\pagebreak
\section*{Airborne lidar data}

The airborne laser scanning (ALS) point cloud data from the "\Sexpr{source_project}" project are described in Table \ref{tab:ALStab} 
and were used to simulate GEDI waveforms coincident with the aforementioned in situ inventory data (Figure \ref{fig:footprintplot}).
At the time of this report, simulated GEDI waveforms have been generated for \Sexpr{n.subplots.als} subplot(s) across \Sexpr{n.plots.als} plot(s),
resulting in \Sexpr{n.filtered.fp} simulated GEDI waveforms after quality filtering (see Table \ref{tab:filtertab}).
This simulator has been validated across a range of forest types and ALS instruments using measured waveforms from 
NASA’s Land, Vegetation and Ice Sensor (LVIS). Figure \ref{fig:footprintplot} illustrates an example of a simulated waveform and derived relative height metrics. 
Relationships between these relative height metrics and the in situ AGBD estimates are shown in Figure \ref{fig:AGBDplot}. 
It is important to note that these bivariate relationships are not indicative of GEDI aboveground biomass model performance. 
This presentation of the data are for visual interpretation and quality control of the project data in context of the entire GEDI FSBD.

